c(1, "header lines 1-7; §2.2 table (verbatim)", "positioning", "Habit Tracker: TheFor (App Store ID 1671322093; subtitle 'Routine Planner, Goal, Journal') by Siraj Hasanov (xyz.thefor.habits.habits), Productivity / Health & Fitness — a small minimalist habit tracker with swipe-to-complete cards, unlimited free habits, flexible frequency, routines, colour-coding and manual order, hide-completed, streaks, back-fill, weekly / monthly heat map, a free home-screen widget, numeric goals, an Explore section of preset routines, reminders, account login, journaling; 80 reviews (every one read), 23 storefronts, 2023-02-25 → 2026-09-02, written mean 4.525 (57×5★, 16×4★, 2×3★, 2×2★, 3×1★); external (lookup API 13 Sep 2026): released 2023-02-24, version 1.4.6 shipped 2025-12-21, free with IAP, English only, age 4+, iOS 13.0+; 267 public ratings across the 23 storefronts (written = 30%); listing (verbatim): " + table("## 2.2 The listed model", 0), "free unlimited habits; Pro $1.99/mo, $9.99/yr, $29.99 lifetime; Routine packs + Routine AI", "praise", "80 reviews; mean 4.525; 267 public ratings", "none", "header", "app-specific", ["9653396257"])
c(2, "How to read this table (verbatim); Seven warnings 1, 2, 3; §1.1 table (verbatim); §1.2; §1.3 table (verbatim); §1.4; §1.5; §1.6; §1.7 table (verbatim); §1.8", "data-caveat", "Method and limits: signal bands (verbatim) " + table("## How to read this", 0) + " — 245 assignments (3.06 per review), 62 codes in 13 families plus 15 unions, read in four chunks of twenty, classification entirely manual (keyword search used only to test negative claims such as 'no review mentions AI'); files (verbatim) " + table("## 1.1 Files used", 0) + "; coverage (verbatim) " + table("## 1.3 Coverage and reconciliation", 0) + "; 29 probed storefronts returned zero reviews (ar au by ci co cr dz gr gt hk il it jo jp kg kh kr lk ma mn pa pe pl sa se si sk uz ye); one author (ShuyinD, de) posted two near-identical 5★ a day apart, both kept and flagged — at n−1 WID_GOOD 4 → 3 and REQ_SYNC 5 → 4, both still above 3%; limitations: one review = 1.25% so a single review clears 'Meaningful'; no storefront reaches 50 (US 14); 30% write rate; positive skew of unknown cause (za written 2.50 vs public 4.40); no version field; 17 non-English reviews read in original; 2023 20 reviews, 2026 4; external data a 13 Sep 2026 snapshot; integrity (verbatim) " + table("## 1.7 Review integrity", 0) + " — no burst; a 2023-04-23→25 cluster (three UK + one US, 4–5★) consistent with a launch push, removing it moves the mean 4.525 → 4.47; one review used as a support ticket, another asks for a support channel", "n/a", "praise", "80 read; 0 eligible storefronts; one review = 1.25%", "research", "method", "generalisable", ["11057937499","11061269605","11580131645"])
c(3, "Warning 3; §4.7; §6.6", "data-caveat", "This corpus is unusually positive and that is the thing to be careful about: 57 of 80 (71.25%) are 5★, 47 (58.75%) contain no complaint or request; written 4.525 vs US public ~4.87 — 'the usual this is what broke reading does not apply', and the 15 negative reviews (18.75%) carry almost all diagnostic weight; META_CONTRA 2 (2.50%) — a 4★ describing a paid subscription that does not work, a failed restore and an unreachable developer ('the clearest single piece of evidence that this corpus's positive skew understates its problems') and a 4★ whose body is '10/10'; public vs written: us 4.87 vs 4.71, th 4.95 vs 4.75, nl 4.93 vs 4.90 — two inversions explained by single reviews (za one billing 1★; de the duplicate pair)", "n/a", "praise", "71.25% 5★; 58.75% no complaint; 30% write rate", "research", "limited evidence", "generalisable", ["9857595761","11431096002","11008247242"])
c(4, "Warning 4; §0.1; §3.4 P2; §7.4 T1; §8.3 M1; §0.10 #3", "product-rule", "The free tier is the product's moat and reviewers say so explicitly: PAY_FREE_UNLIMITED 10 (12.50%, high-priority, mean 4.80) name the competitor behaviour it avoids — 'a maioria dos apps permitem de 3 a 5 itens de lista e so liberam mais no premium, esse tem quantidade de hábitos ilimitados no plano free'; 'I love that you can have as many tasks as you want which is rare for free apps'; 'If you don't want to pay for subscription, this app will still be functional and will NOT limit the amount of habits you can add (I've been looking for this 😭)'; 'o único aplicativo que encontrei que não limita' (2026); free-offer praise union (unlimited habits, generous free tier, no ads, no upgrade nagging) 19 (23.75%, mean 4.89 — the highest-rated theme family; none below 4★, 18 at 5★); T1 rising strongly — free_tier_praise 5.0% (1/20) → 23.3% (10/43) → 47.1% (8/17), PAY_FREE_UNLIMITED 5.0% → 9.3% → 29.4% — 'what a differentiator looks like when competitors move the other way'; flat across market groups (25.0% vs 23.2%) — 'not a developing-market story or a rich-market story'; the listing promises 'Unlimited Habit Creation' and zero reviewers complain of a cap — 'the habit cap is not a monetization lever available to this product. It is the acquisition story'; M1: publicly commit to unlimited free habits", "unlimited habits free", "5★-burst", "PAY_FREE_UNLIMITED 10 (12.50%) 4.80; free union 19 (23.75%) 4.89; 5.0% → 29.4%", "product-rule", "high-priority", "generalisable", ["12389094071","10550235895","11504813604","11833253847","13583194808","14189467986"])
c(5, "§0.2; §3.3 N1; §7.4 T4; §8.2 B1; §8.5 X1; §0.10 #1", "feature", "Cross-device sync is the one thing people reduce the rating for: sync_any 5 (6.25%, high-priority, mean 4.20), 3 of them tried it and found it broken (BUG_SYNC 3, 3.75%, mean 3.67) — the corpus's only 3★ ('Love that the free version includes unlimited habits. And the paid version is a great price. However, needs to be able to sync across devices'), two 4★ ('i've tried logging on and off and deleting and reinstalling the app but nothing works :/'; 'не могу синхронизировать его работу на двух устройствах — iPhone и iPad'), two 5★ from the same reviewer ('the lack of iCloud sync … a notable drawback'); every one praises the app in the same breath — 'a gap that costs stars from people who already like the product, which is the cheapest kind of rating to recover'; an account system exists but data does not follow it; rising 0.0% → 7.0% → 11.8% while the corpus shrinks; not in the listing, so users are not mis-sold; data_continuity union 7 (8.75%, mean 3.86); B1: iCloud iPhone ↔ iPad sync; X1: does sync convert — ship multi-device in Pro and measure attach rate", "absent / broken", "complaint", "sync_any 5 (6.25%) 4.20; BUG_SYNC 3 (3.75%) 3.67; 0% → 7.0% → 11.8%", "build-paid", "high-priority (n=5)", "generalisable", ["12454850679","12090413380","12912139905","11057937499","11061269605"])
c(6, "Warning 6; §0.3 table (verbatim); §3.3 N2; §5.1 table (verbatim); §5.5 table (verbatim); §8.1 F1, F2; §8.7 #1; §0.10 #2", "must-never-break", "Three of the four people who say they paid describe a failure (PAY_PAID 4, 5.00%, mean 2.75 vs 4.525; payer 2.75 vs non-payer 4.62 — 75% segment rate on four people, global 3.75%) (verbatim): " + table("## 0.3 Three of the four people", 0) + " — two describe the same defect from different angles, the app does not reliably restore a purchase: 'I payed for an annual subscription but the app is still prompting me to pay. Hitting restore purchase does not help'; 'Eu comprei o app. Desinstalei e na hora que fui instalar novamente, sumiu tudo o q estava lá e pediu novamente para comprar' (data gone and asked to pay again; titled 'Problemas com sincronização'); BUG_RESTORE 2 (2.50%, mean 3.00), BUG_DATA_LOSS 1; 22 months apart on different storefronts — 'a persistent weakness in the receipt-validation / restore path', not a release regression; 'the paid path is the only part of this product with a majority-failure account, and it is the part that generates revenue'; payers (verbatim): " + table("## 5.1 Who the paying reviewers are", 0) + " || post-purchase (verbatim): " + table("## 5.5 Post-purchase problems", 0) + " — no refund described as granted or refused; F1: validate the receipt on launch, never show a paywall to a Pro owner, show entitlement state in-app; F2: never lose local data on reinstall", "restore fails; reinstall wipes data + entitlement", "1★-burst", "4 payers @ 2.75; 3/4 failure; BUG_RESTORE 2", "must-never-break", "limited evidence (segment n=4)", "generalisable", ["9857595761","12310524086","11008247242","11778005498"])
c(7, "§0.4; §3.3 N3; §8.1 F3; §8.7 #2; §0.10 #4", "must-never-break", "Notifications — not many complaints, but the ones there are are total: BUG_NOTIF 2 (2.50%, mean 2.50) — 'I am unable to receive any notifications acb you help.? It's really annoying' (in, 1★ — the corpus's only bug-driven 1★); 'I unabled notificafions when I first downloaded the app and now I can not activate it on app or system notificafions' (tr, 4★) — a user who declines the iOS permission prompt at first run has no in-app path back; 'For a habit tracker, a user in this state has a reminder-less product'; F3: detect denied authorisation status, show an explanatory row, deep-link to iOS Settings (openSettingsURLString)", "no permission recovery path", "1★-burst", "BUG_NOTIF 2 (2.50%) 2.50", "must-never-break", "meaningful (n=2)", "generalisable", ["11037267664","11830513457"])
c(8, "§0.5; §3.3 N4; §8.1 F4; §8.2 B3; §0.10 #5", "must-never-break", "Progress and analytics are the thin edge of the product: progress_views_neg 4 (5.00%, very strong, mean 3.50) against TRK_OVERVIEW praise 4 (5.00%, 4.75) — four different problems: the heat map is 'quite gimmicky' and a day cannot be tapped to see which habits were done (REQ_DAY_DETAIL); stats, day history and back-fill moved behind a subscription; 'só sinto muita falta de análise de dados, gráficos dos hábitos, como no aplicativo concorrente Ripples' (the only named competitor); and correctness — 'Even though I completed around 75% of my test, only 20%. Why?' (3★, 2026-03-20, BUG_ANALYTICS — the most recent negative review and the only open 2026 bug); the listing promises 'Comprehensive Weekly Overview' and 'Track Your Habit History … Gain valuable insights'; F4: verify the completion percentage first — 'A wrong number in the one screen that reports progress undermines every other claim'; B3 per-day detail and charts only after F4 — 'Deepening a view that computes the wrong number is the wrong order'", "heat map only; % wrong", "complaint", "progress_neg 4 (5.00%) 3.50; overview praise 4", "must-never-break", "very strong (n=4)", "generalisable", ["10147768318","11961668175","13583194808","13868883595","11669968530"])
c(9, "§0.6 table (verbatim); §7.4 T2; §8.1 F5; §8.2 B2; §0.10 #6", "timeline", "The widget request was shipped, and the corpus records the whole arc (verbatim): " + table("## 0.6 The widget request was shipped", 0) + " — REQ_WIDGET 20.0% (2023) → 0.0% (2024) → 5.9% (2025–26); WID_GOOD 4 (5.00%, mean 5.00: 'there's a cute widget I can put on my home screen as the cherry on top'; 'having the free widget is awesome'); defects found (BUG_WIDGET 2: won't launch the app unless already backgrounded; doesn't show already-completed tasks — refresh / state bugs); the next ask is interactive: 'I'd like a widget that allows me to see all my habits and their progress and allows me to check them off' (2026-09-02, the most recent review) — 'the best evidence that this developer ships against review feedback'; F5 fix the two widget defects; B2 an interactive widget (iOS 17+) with check-off", "widget shipped free Dec 2023", "praise", "REQ_WIDGET 20.0% → 0.0% → 5.9%; WID_GOOD 4 @ 5.00", "build-free", "very strong", "generalisable", ["10317711703","10426368892","10550235895","10630906608","10775562864","12643553324","11307114339","11792629969","14500803900"])
c(10, "§0.7; §2.4; §3.3 N7; §8.3 M2, M3; §8.6 #6; part 8 #6", "timeline", "The one monetization backlash, and why the corpus does not corroborate it: 'app fell off when you introduced a paid subscription to be able to view stats of habit tracking or just not even able to see which days were tracked, and to try and track previous days u might've forgotten to … You prided yourself on offering a great app with absolutely no payment or prices for subscription for stats … Now you're just like everything else' (gb, 2★, 2024-11-17, 'having the app for years and getting attached to it 💔') — PAY_PAYWALL_REGRESSION 1 (1.25%); counter-evidence: in the 20 reviews on or after that date free-tier praise is 40.0% (8/20) and unlimited-habits praise 25.0% (5/20), higher than the 60 before (18.3% and 8.3%) — whatever moved behind the paywall, 'it was not the habit cap'; the 2026 listing still advertises weekly overview and habit history and a 2024-08 review praises 'good stats' — three readings (paywall added then relaxed; depth gated while a basic view stayed free; one user hit a bug); 'one long-tenured user lost a specific capability (stats + back-fill) and left. That is a retention story worth one engineer-day'; M2: build Pro from additive capability, never by removing free capability; M3: audit what is actually gated and reconcile with the listing — 'the single highest-value thing to check'; research #6", "stats / back-fill reportedly gated late 2024", "churn", "1 review; later free praise 40.0% vs 18.3% before", "product-rule", "limited evidence (n=1)", "generalisable", ["11961668175","11669968530","10317711703"])
c(11, "§0.8; §2.3 table (verbatim); §8.3 M4; §0.10 #7", "monetization", "Two revenue lines are invisible in the corpus: six IAP lines — Pro Month $1.99, Pro Year $9.99, Pro Year With Trial $9.99, Pro Lifetime $29.99, Routine AI $2.99, 'Routine' $0.99 / $1.99 / $2.99 — and across all 80 reviews zero mention AI in any form and zero mention buying a routine pack; the Explore / preset-routine surface appears three times: 'I am struggling to find the section of exploring popular routines' (cannot find it); 'It would be nice if there was more content in the explore part' (too thin); 'You can even copy habits that are already in the app and add them to your own routine' (the only one who found it useful); 'A paid content catalogue that no reviewer has ever mentioned buying, attached to a surface that one reviewer cannot locate and another finds empty, is either pre-revenue or mis-placed'; zero reviews mention a trial though a trial SKU exists; free / paid (verbatim): " + table("## 2.3 Free / paid / trial / unclear", 0) + " — M4: decide whether Routine / Routine AI is a business — make it findable and stocked, or remove it", "Routine packs + Routine AI listed, never mentioned", "none", "0 of 80 mention AI or routine purchase; UX_FIND 1; REQ_EXPLORE_CONTENT 1", "research", "limited evidence", "generalisable", ["11293453970","12643553324","12489656823"])
c(12, "§0.9 table (verbatim); §2.5; §3.4 P3; §8.4 P2", "positioning", "What the app is loved for, in order (verbatim): " + table("## 0.9 What the app is loved for", 0) + " — 19 reviewers (23.75%, mean 4.84) explicitly tried other habit trackers and kept this one: 'I've tried almost 10 apps. While I deleted all others instantly because they didn't meet my requirements for a simple solution'; 'You don't know how many habit tracker apps I tried before finding this one'; 'I've made habit trackers on notion and even used other habit tracker apps'; 'it's better than so many of the other more expensive paid apps' (COMP_VS_PAID 2) — 'The buyer this app wins is a habit-tracker refugee: someone who has already churned out of two to ten competitors and is looking for less product, not more'; only one competitor named — Ripples, for better charts; P2: market to habit-tracker refugees — the listing sells 'Transform Your Life'; the corpus says people buy relief from other apps", "minimal tracker", "praise", "COMP_BEST 19 (23.75%) 4.84", "do", "high-priority", "generalisable", ["10180848573","10657538444","10798954077","11136791730","10953962678","11669968530"])
c(13, "§3.4 P1 table (verbatim); §8.4 P1; §8.7 closing", "product-rule", "Design — simple, good-looking, easy — is the single largest theme: design_praise 39 (48.75%, high-priority, mean 4.74) (verbatim): " + table("### P1 — Design", 0) + " — the language is uniform and negative about competitors: 'No bloatware, no hassle'; 'No extra junk!'; 'without all the extra bells and whistles'; 'simple, well designed, no gimmicks'; 'ничего лишнего, только то, что нужно'; 'No need to waste your time to learn new apps' — 'This is a defended position, not a compliment. 25 people chose this product because of what it does not have'; 'Adding capability is how this product loses the position it holds'; P1: every build item ships behind a setting or inside an existing screen, not as a new tab — 'nothing on this list should add a tab. 31.25% of this corpus chose the app for what it does not have'", "minimal", "praise", "39 (48.75%) 4.74; DES_SIMPLE 25 (31.25%) 4.84", "product-rule", "high-priority", "generalisable", ["9858788960","9803618820","10798954077","10630906608","11426505951","13205717445"])
c(14, "§3.4 P2; §8.3 M5", "product-rule", "Behaviour the app refrains from is praised: PAY_NO_NAG — 'Even better - there's no constant barrage of prompts asking you to upgrade!'; PAY_NOADS — 'Es genial y no tiene anuncios'; zero reviewers in 80 report seeing an ad; M5: do not add ads — they would attack DES_SIMPLE (25) and free_tier_praise (19), the two largest positive themes", "no ads; no upgrade nagging", "praise", "PAY_NO_NAG 1; PAY_NOADS 1; 0 ad sightings", "product-rule", "limited evidence", "generalisable", ["10798954077","11146415478"])
c(15, "§3.3 N5; §3.4 P6; §8.1 F7; §8.5 X2; §8.7 #3", "must-have", "Support reachability — the developer responds but cannot be found: 'Unable to contact developer on their website'; 'Let me know if I can email the suggestions' (a 4★ with feedback and nowhere to send it); a 1★ titled 'Phishing spam scam' demanding cancellation 'confirmed in writing' — 'where people go when they believe no private channel exists'; against SUP_GOOD 2 (mean 5.00): 'I reported a bug and the developers responded quickly and resolved the bug soon after. A+ response'; 'the developer reacts quickly to feedback' — 'a support-surface problem, not a support-quality problem'; F7: an email link on settings and a 'Manage subscription' row deep-linking to Apple; X2: does a visible support route reduce 1★ — two of three 1★ describe problems a support conversation resolves", "no in-app support route", "1★-burst", "SUP_UNREACHABLE 1; SUP_CHANNEL 1; SUP_GOOD 2 @ 5.00", "must-have", "limited evidence", "generalisable", ["9857595761","11669968530","11008247242","11402240653","11061269605"])
